      "worked": "Both logarithms must be defined, so $x+3>0$ and $3-x>0$. Hence $-3<x<3$.\n\nAt the intersection, the ordinates are equal. Change to base 2:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_2(x+3)&=\\log_4(3-x)\\\\\\log_2(x+3)&=\\frac{\\log_2(3-x)}{\\log_2(4)}\\\\2\\log_2(x+3)&=\\log_2(3-x)\\\\\\log_2\\bigl((x+3)^2\\bigr)&=\\log_2(3-x)\\\\(x+3)^2&=3-x\\\\x^2+7x+6&=0\\\\(x+1)(x+6)&=0\\\\x&=-1\\text{ or }x=-6\\end{align*}$$\n\nOnly $x=-1$ satisfies $-3<x<3$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\log_2(-1+3)\\\\y&=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore $P=(-1,1)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
